+
+## SMS verification for sign-up
+
+Set `PUBLIC_SMS_SEND_URL` and `PUBLIC_SMS_VERIFY_URL` at build time (see `.env.example`). These must point to your SMS backend; this repository does not include an SMS provider or verification service. Without them, the form reports that phone verification is unavailable and does not register an unverified account.
+
+The frontend uses the following JSON contract:
+
+| Endpoint | POST request | Successful JSON response |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `PUBLIC_SMS_SEND_URL` | `{ "phoneNumber": "+12025550123" }` | `{ "challengeId": "opaque-challenge-id" }` |
+| `PUBLIC_SMS_VERIFY_URL` | `{ "phoneNumber": "+12025550123", "challengeId": "opaque-challenge-id", "code": "123456" }` | `{ "verificationToken": "opaque-server-proof" }` |
+| Existing `/api/register` | `{ "username": "reader", "password": "…", "phoneNumber": "+12025550123", "verificationToken": "opaque-server-proof" }` | A successful HTTP status |
+
+The registration backend must validate the verification token, bind it to the submitted number, and reject registration without valid proof. Configure CORS for the app origin when these endpoints are cross-origin. The SMS backend must enforce code expiry, attempt limits and send rate limits; the form's 30-second resend timer is only a UI convenience. Verification tokens must remain valid for registration retries and be consumed on successful account creation. No credentials or verification tokens are persisted by the frontend.
+
+Use six-digit numeric codes. For [WebOTP automatic extraction](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp), serve the app over HTTPS and end the SMS with the actual page hostname (no scheme, path or port), a space, and `#` followed by the code:
+
+```text
+Your DevTools Times verification code is 123456.
+
+@your-app.example #123456
+```
+
+The form starts listening before requesting the SMS and cancels listening on submission, editing, timeout or unmount. It fills the code after browser consent; the user confirms submission. The single labeled code input also supports `autocomplete="one-time-code"`, numeric keyboards, leading zeros, pasting, and manual entry when WebOTP is unavailable.
